node_modules/
*.log
# pebbl's own store, in SHARED mode — the same line set `pebbl init --shared`
# writes, because pebbl should live under its own convention rather than a
# bespoke one. events.jsonl is the single committed source of truth; everything
# below is derived from it and rebuilds on the next read, so committing any of
# it would store the same fact twice and hand git a binary it cannot merge.
#
# Files are ignored explicitly BY NAME rather than blanket-ignoring `.pebbl/`:
# git does not descend into a blanket-ignored directory, so a `!` negation
# inside one is inert. Keeping the directory un-ignored is what leaves
# events.jsonl and .events-canonical tracked by default.
#
# events.local.jsonl is the private half of the two-file split. The fold unions
# it in locally; git only ever carries events.jsonl. On a PUBLIC remote,
# foundation entries route here by default — which is what makes it safe for
# this store to live in a public repo at all.
.pebbl/events.local.jsonl
.pebbl/view.sqlite
.pebbl/db.sqlite
.pebbl/manual-logs.md
.pebbl/handoffs.md
.pebbl/commit-log.md
.pebbl/narrative.md
.pebbl/events-view.md
.pebbl/*.lock
.pebbl/.rebuild-needed
.DS_Store
# pnpm is the single source of truth (see package.json packageManager +
# pnpm-workspace.yaml security config). Don't let `npm install` re-add its lockfile.
package-lock.json
